  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "TCP: Follow: Use the ports and addresses from the TCP header",
  "description": "Instead of using pinfo->{src,dest}port and pinfo->{src,dst},\nuse the values for the TCP ports and addresses from the tcpheader\nstructure passed in the follow_data to the follow tap. The later\nis the value at the time of tapping and thus the correct value for\nthe TCP segment passed to the follow tap; the value in the packet_info\nstruct is the value at the *end* of dissection, and is not necessarily\nthe same if any later dissector changed the addresses or ports.\n\nIn particular, this is a reason why the packet_info struct has\nspecial entries for clnp_srcref and clnp_dstref instead of putting them\ninto the standard port values; it can also affect other tunneling.\n\nPing #18231\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
